php7.4 composer.phar install
API_KEY='replace-with-a-long-random-secret' php7.4 -S 0.0.0.0:8000
dont forget to create db

Phinx is configured in phinx.php. Composer installs Phinx but does not generate
its configuration. Set PHINX_DB_PASSWORD in the shell (and override other
PHINX_DB_* values if needed), then run:

PHINX_DB_PASSWORD='your-database-password' php7.4 vendor/bin/phinx migrate

to serve from apache2 need to use following apache2 config:

<VirtualHost *:8005>
    ServerName 192.168.1.111
    DocumentRoot /home/rafal/polaris/backend
    DirectoryIndex index.php
    SetEnv API_KEY "replace-with-a-long-random-secret"

    <Directory /home/rafal/polaris/backend>
        Options -Indexes +FollowSymLinks
        AllowOverride All
        Require all granted
    </Directory>

    <Directory /home/rafal/polaris/backend/protected>
        Require all denied
    </Directory>

    ErrorLog ${APACHE_LOG_DIR}/polaris_error.log
    CustomLog ${APACHE_LOG_DIR}/polaris_access.log combined
</VirtualHost>

./backend/protected/runtime and /backend/assets need to be chown by www-data

All /api endpoints require the X-API-Key request header. Configure the expected
key as the API_KEY environment variable for the PHP process. For Apache, SetEnv
can be used as shown above; keep the real key in deployment configuration, not
in source control. Requests without a valid key receive HTTP 401. If API_KEY is
unset or empty, API requests fail closed with HTTP 500.
Treat the API key as a bearer credential and expose the API over HTTPS in
production.

Example request:

curl -H 'X-API-Key: dlgjh2hyeuihdbn13or794yghn2o3p=eif' \
  'http://localhost:8000/api/users'

JSON API routes accept parameters in a JSON object request body for all HTTP
methods. For GET requests, query parameters remain supported as a fallback.
Send `Content-Type: application/json`; form-encoded POST fields are not read.

GET    /api/users                         Optional id selects one user.
POST   /api/user                          name, email, password.
PUT    /api/user                          id and any fields to update.
DELETE /api/user                          id.
GET    /api/chat_users                    Optional username selects one chat user.
GET    /api/chat_user                     username.
POST   /api/chat_user                     username.
DELETE /api/chat_user                     Deletes all chat users.
GET    /api/chat_user_last_activity       username query parameter.
PUT    /api/chat_user_last_activity       username and last_activity.
GET    /api/user_messages                 username query parameter.
GET    /api/user_message_created_on       id query parameter.
PUT    /api/user_message_created_on       id and created_on.
POST   /api/user_message                  from_user and message.

Note: GET request bodies are not supported consistently by all HTTP clients and
intermediaries; query parameters are the interoperable option for GET selectors.

