NBA data model (migrations + seed)

Order: php8.3 vendor/bin/phinx migrate  (applies 20261023120000 reference tables,
20261023120100 players, 20261023120200 stats/games, in that order), then
php8.3 vendor/bin/phinx seed:run -s NbaSeeder
NbaSeeder is idempotent (upserts on external ids / unique keys) and can be re-run.
It loads 30 teams, stadiums, 30 head coaches, positions (ESPN's G/F/C only) and the
516 players on ESPN's 2026-27 rosters as observed 2026-10-23 (data in
db/seeds/data/nba_2026_27.php; sources are listed in the NbaSeeder docblock).
Not seeded (no sourced data): two-way/contract type (players.contract_type is NULL =
unknown), prior teams, season/career stats, games, game stats, champions.
ActiveRecord models are the *Record classes in protected/App_Code (relations are
declared in each class's $RELATIONS). Stat column is totalRebounds.

The authenticated page ?page=PlayerGridDevExtreme is a DevExtreme DataGrid
version of ?page=PlayerGrid. It loads the same player data and supports sorting,
filtering, paging, and instant multi-selection across pages. Select all applies
to the current grid filter. The selected player IDs are displayed as an array.
Selection is client-side and resets on reload; changing the grid filter does not
clear it.
As in PlayerGrid, the team name is hidden for selected rows.
Players whose last name is Williams or Willams (case-insensitive, ignoring
surrounding whitespace) remain visible but cannot be selected, including when
selecting all rows across pages.
This page loads DevExtreme 24.2.7 from the DevExpress CDN and requires network
access and an appropriate DevExtreme license.
